# OpenFlaps {{VERSION}} — hardware kit

OpenFlaps is a networked split-flap display you build yourself: 3D-printed characters,
each driven by a small stepper motor and its own ATtiny84 board, chained to a Raspberry Pi
Pico W controller with a web interface. Show the time, the date, the weather, reminders,
or any text you like.

## What's in this folder

- `guides/`: the print guide and the assembly guide, as PDFs.
- `stl/`: every 3D-printed part.
- `stl/flaps/`: the 45 character flaps, as two-colour 3MF files (white characters on black).
- `pcb/`: Gerbers, bills of materials and pick-and-place files for the three boards.
- `photos/`: pictures of a finished display (when included).
- `LICENSE-models.md` and `LICENSE`: the licenses (see below).

## Where to start

1. Read `guides/OpenFlaps-Print-Guide.pdf` and print the parts.
2. Order the boards from `pcb/` (any PCB fab works; see `pcb/README.md`).
3. Follow `guides/OpenFlaps-Assembly-Guide.pdf` step by step.

## Firmware and software

The firmware (Pico W and ATtiny84) and the web interface are not in this kit. Get them from
the repository, at the same version as this kit:

